      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143459",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$f(x, y) = {1,\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x < 1, x - 1 < y < 1 - x \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x)$ for $0 < x < 1, x - 1 < y < 1 - x$."
